      "id": "balis",
      "end": 1599,
      "contributors": [],
      "provenance": "Pleiades",
      "associationCertaintyURI": "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/association-certainty/certain",
      "start": 1500,
      "details": "<p class=\"p1\"><em>B\u0101l\u012bs</em>:\u00a0It is a small town on the <em>Fur\u0101t</em> (Euphrates) belonging to <em>C\u00fcnd \u1e32\u0131nnesr\u012bn</em> (the district of Qinnasr\u012bn), and serves as a river port. Merchants coming from <em>M\u0131\u1e63r</em> (Egypt) and <em>diy\u0101r-\u0131 \u015e\u0101m</em> (Bil\u0101d al-Sh\u0101m / Greater Syria) would embark on their boats at that place. They would send their goods to <em>Ba\u0121d\u0101d</em> (Baghdad) from that station.\u00a0When the Melik\u00fc\u2019n-n\u0101\u1e63\u0131r \u1e62al\u0101\u1e25a\u2019d-d\u012bn (Salah al-Din) came to power, the waters of the Euphrates receded from <em>B\u0101l\u012bs</em>. Because of this,\u00a0<em>Eb\u016b Bekr bin \u1e32\u0131v\u0101m-\u0131 B\u0101l\u012bs\u012b</em> (Ab\u016b Bekr b. \u1e32iv\u0101m al-B\u0101l\u012bs\u012b), one of the ascetics, diverted a canal from the Euphrates to <em>B\u0101l\u012bs</em>. For a long time, the people of the region benefitted from it. Afterwards, that too fell into ruin, and the town of <em>B\u0101l\u012bs</em> became deserted.\u00a0The people of <em>B\u0101l\u012bs</em> are known for lack of sense and stupidity. [translation]</p>",
      "review_state": "published",
